        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "254755a6-c547-5530-92e7-a06316a55acf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lorde, Joel Little\n- Songs: \"Tennis Court\", \"Royals\", \"Mother Mother\", \"Heartlines\"\n- Albums and EPs: \"The Love Club EP\", \"Pure Heroine\"\n- Companies: Universal Music Group\n- Charts: Billboard Alternative Songs\n\nFacts:\n- \"Royals\" is a song by New Zealand singer Lorde from her debut EP \"The Love Club EP\" released in 2012.\n- \"Royals\" was later included on Lorde's debut studio album \"Pure Heroine\" in 2013.\n- On 7 June 2013, Universal Music Group released \"Tennis Court\" as the second single from \"Pure Heroine\", following \"Royals\".\n- In August 2013, \"Royals\" by Lorde became the first song by a female solo artist to top the renamed Billboard Alternative Songs chart since \"Mother Mother\".\n- \"Heartlines\" was co-written by New Zealand musician Lorde and its producer Joel Little.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
